{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"5bfc2ad1c5a4d425c97eb5591d5e23465e02c3370f19406aef53f9256022be7a","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion-verification gate","key_entities":["CompletionVerdict","SCHEMA_PASS","completion_verifier_pass_v1","Criterion","criteria[]","completion_sidecar.py","reconcile_verdict","completion-verification.yaml","gate_ops.py","completion_verifier.md"],"problem_keywords":["completion verification","per-criterion audit","pass record persistence","lossless verdict tracking","sidecar emission"],"propositions":["Completion verification currently emits findings only on FAIL; a successful PASS leaves no durable per-criterion audit record, unlike plan and code reviews.","The verifier must emit a populated criteria array with one met-record per evaluated criterion (including met status, citation, and kind) on PASS, alongside an empty findings list.","A new completion_verifier_pass_v1 schema and sidecar record must persist the per-criterion array, verdict, runner, model, and material fingerprint on PASS only.","The pydantic CompletionVerdict model must declare a Criterion sub-model and criteria field to prevent pydantic v2 from dropping the agent-emitted criteria array.","The criteria array must flow end-to-end through the workflow (verify step → reconcile step → close gate) and survive in the reconciled verdict without being stripped or flipped to FAIL."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785825070573435743,"uuid":"ed7a5422-0f00-4895-867c-c01401207241"}